# Markdown output conventions

- Prefer GitHub-flavored Markdown (GFM) for all formatted output: docs,
  READMEs, chat responses, generated reports.
- Never embed images as base64 data URLs in Markdown files. GitHub's
  renderer strips `data:` image URIs, and multi-hundred-KB single-line
  embeds break other previewers. Use committed relative-path files
  instead (e.g. `docs/src/screenshots/*.jpg`).

```markdown
<!-- ❌ BAD: stripped by GitHub, breaks previewers -->
![home](data:image/jpeg;base64,/9j/4AAQ...)

<!-- ✅ GOOD: relative path to a committed asset -->
![home](docs/src/screenshots/home-route.jpg)

<!-- ✅ GOOD: HTML img when a display width is needed -->
<img src="docs/src/screenshots/home-route.jpg" alt="home" width="480">
```

- Exception: tiny icons inside SVG/HTML assets (not Markdown) may use
  data URLs, as `scripts/update-logo.sh` does for generated SVGs.
- Markdown pipe tables render a horizontal rule from the header row; for
  header-less layout grids (like the README hero), use an HTML `<table>`.
